rect_ship_2026-08-11 — the rectangle's t=1 cost, located; and the CDEF sites priced
====================================================================================

Branch      perf/rect-ship, base e351b1a (PR #505 merged)
Host        Apple M4 Pro, 8P + 4E, macOS 26.5.2, aarch64
Toolchain   stable-aarch64-apple-darwin, no -C target-cpu=native
Harness     scripts/perf/tiled_wallcpu.sh under ~/bin/measlock, NEVER niced
Report      scripts/perf/rect_report.py (paired per-round ratios, round 0
            dropped as cold, whole rounds dropped when any arm saw a foreign
            process above 25% CPU)
Fit         total = a + b*frames at two frame counts per cell, so process
            startup / mmap / decoder construction drop out of wall AND CPU
Static      scripts/perf/text_layout_diff.py, scripts/perf/text_symbol_diff.sh,
            cargo llvm-lines
Full write-up  docs/RECT_SHIP.md

VERDICT
-------
NOTHING SHIPS. The default is unchanged and verified byte-equivalent to the base
commit's build (__text 1,839,536 -> 1,839,536, 0 symbols resized, 0 added).

#505's blocking result — +1.0..+1.3% wall at t=1 on `v4k8tile`, 0/11 twice,
where the rectangle path never executes — is CODE PLACEMENT, not the mechanism.
4,828 bytes of provably-dead `#[used]` text, in a build where NO symbol changes
size and every hot loop-filter symbol's disassembly is byte-identical, costs
+1.10% wall, 0 of 11. Nine binaries differing from main's by +1,132 B to
+19,420 B all land in +1.1%..+1.6% with 9/9-0/11 signs; a byte-identical copy
reads 1.0006 (4/11). Against a SAME-SOURCE control the rectangle costs nothing
at t=1: 0.9967, 7/9.

The round's acceptance bar (t=1 inside +-0.5% of main, coin-flip sign, n>=11) is
therefore not met by ANY arm, including arms that change no executed instruction
anywhere, so per the brief the default was not flipped.

THE OTHER NUMBER THE ROUND EXISTS FOR (task 2)
----------------------------------------------
RAV1D_CDEF_DOUBLE (--features __probe_cdef_double) prices the five CDEF
registration sites docs/RECT_RECORDS.md 7b named, in ONE binary, by doubling
them. Marginal price 3.27 ns/registration on c256x2048 t=8 (+159,424 regs/frame,
+1.34% wall, CPU sign 0/13) and 5.27 ns on c1024x576 t=8 (+121,856 regs/frame,
+4.09% wall, 0/12). Null control: text_q20 files ZERO CDEF registrations and the
arm reads wall 1.0000 (5/12).
=> On c256x2048 the sites are 28.0% of the population and 4.6% of that cell's
   11.23 CPU ms/frame tracker (tracker CPU CITED from docs/C256_CONTENTION.md 7,
   not re-measured). 7b guessed ~2.7%.
=> On c1024x576 they are +4.09% of WALL, far above 7b's "under ~1% => nothing to
   win". A rectangle collapses 8 rows to 1, so the arithmetic ceiling there is
   ~3.6% wall, on the same cell family where the fill rectangle already delivers
   -1.7%..-2.4%. NOT REFUTED; the better target than c256x2048 ever was.
=> Standing caveat: fill's own doubling priced its population at +3.37% wall on
   c256x2048 and the actual collapse delivered ~0 there. A doubling is an UPPER
   BOUND on what a collapse buys.

ARMS (all verified to emit ONE md5 per (cell, threads) before any timing)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
plain      base-commit default codegen (the binary main ships)
plainB     byte-identical copy of plain
pad1..4    plain + 4,828 / 9,692 / 14,556 / 19,420 bytes of never-called
           #[used] text in src/loopfilter.rs (feature __pad_text/__pad2/3/4).
           text_layout_diff.py: resized_in_both = 0 in every rung
rect       #505's arm: --features __lf_rect at its final (inline(never)) shape
plain2     the fill/fill_threaded split, DEFAULT features: +5,176 B of new
           out-of-line functions, -4,044 B from the two LfBlock::open, net +1,132
plain2B    byte-identical copy of plain2
padsmall   plain2 + 2,348 B of dead text (feature __pad_small)
padfar     plain2 + 5,996 B of dead text emitted from src/text_pad.rs
           (feature __pad_far) — a second module, NOT a location control: the
           linker still places it before the loop-filter block
ship       plain2 + --features __lf_rect
cdefoff/on ONE binary (--features __probe_cdef_double), RAV1D_CDEF_DOUBLE 0/1
cdefoff2   a third alias of that binary with the same environment (A/A control)

